{"actor":{"id":"claude-fable-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"All three audits are in, all findings fixed, and all suites re-verified green (annals 150, cledger 90, turnbridge 91).\n\n## Audit results (three sonnet agents, one per repo)\n\n**annals vs the old store layer** — the deep one. Six files byte-identical, the rest only intended changes, except **four real bugs, all now fixed**:\n1. The scan gate's temp ref was still hardcoded `conversation-ledger-scan-tmp` (would collide across namespaces) → now namespaced.\n2. `ScanBlockedError`'s message had lost its CLI-name prefix entirely → now takes the namespace's CLI name.\n3. The worst one: `cledger review`'s redaction path **persisted** `reason: \"cledger review\"` into the redaction event — wrong provenance stored forever under any other namespace → now interpolates the namespace CLI. Also a hardcoded message string.\n4. Config-file warnings (`cledger: ignoring …`) weren't namespaced → fixed.\n\nPlus two cosmetic report-formatting fixes, and one design note now documented in the README: with two namespaces in one repo, only the first pre-push hook block sees git's pushed-ref stdin; later blocks degrade to HEAD scope (push still happens).\n\n**cledger rewire** — no dropped features: every public export from main survives, the rename never touched content payloads or source-format keys, CLI semantics equivalent. One real finding to remember: the `file:../annals` dependency makes conversation-ledger **unpublishable to npm** until annals is published and the dep becomes a version range.\n\n**turnbridge** — fully clean; the lineage payload keys (`source_conversation`, `imported_through_seq`) were correctly untouched. One inert `ev1-test-` literal in a test fixture, cosmetic.\n\n## Smoke tests: yes, they were needed — one caught a real regression\n\nUnit tests never exercise the *installed* artifacts or the upgrade path, so I ran three scenarios in throwaway temp repos with isolated `$HOME`:\n\n1. **Fresh cledger end-to-end**: library append → hook + refspec auto-installed (pointing at cledger's own cli.js, correct guard var) → `cledger log/show/export` render → plain `git push` carried the notes ref to a bare origin → `scan` clean. Passed — after catching that **the fetch refspec's staging ref had silently changed** (`cledger-incoming` → `conversation-ledger-incoming`), which would have left a duplicate refspec and an orphaned staging ref in all nine of your real repos. Fixed by adding `incomingName` to `NamespaceConfig`; cledger pins its historical name, so existing configs are recognized as already-installed.\n2. **Upgrade from a pre-extraction repo**: real old hook block + old refspec + a hand-written ev1 note → one append upgraded the hook in place (user's surrounding lines preserved, no duplicate block, new guard var), recognized the old refspec (no duplicate), and `log` rendered the ev1 event alongside a new ev2 event without erroring. Passed.\n3. **Namespace coexistence**: cledger's namespace plus a custom `intent-recall` namespace in one repo — separate refs, isolated reads, wiping one ref leaves the other. Passed, with the documented caveat that a custom namespace's hook needs its CLI on PATH or an explicit `hookInvocation` to auto-push.\n\nEverything is committed on the same local branches as before (annals `main` now 3 commits, cledger `annals-extraction`, turnbridge `annals-cledger`); nothing pushed, wipe script still untouched and waiting for you.\n\nresult: Audits found and I fixed 4 real namespacing bugs in annals (worst: wrong tool name persisted into redaction events) plus a refspec regression the smoke tests caught (staging-ref rename that would have polluted all nine repos); smoke tests were worth it — fresh install, pre-extraction upgrade, and two-namespace coexistence all pass end-to-end, and all 331 tests across the three repos are green.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"annals-extraction","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/r