{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"attachment":{"filename":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/README.md","snippet":"53\t\n54\tEvery operation takes a `Ledger` — a repo handle plus a namespace — from\n55\t`openLedger(repo, opts)`. A namespace picks the notes ref\n56\t(`refs/notes/<name>`), the state directory under `.git`, the config file\n57\tname, and the CLI the pre-push hook invokes. Producers that want their own\n58\tindependently-pushable, independently-wipeable ref (a derived layer that must\n59\tbe rebuildable, say) open their own namespace; producers extending an\n60\texisting vocabulary write into that vocabulary's namespace through its\n61\towner's API. cledger uses `{ name: \"conversation-ledger\", configFile: \".cledger.json\" }`.\n62\t\n63\tTwo namespaces in one repo chain two hook blocks in `pre-push`. Git feeds\n64\tthat script its stdin once, so only the first block sees the pushed-ref\n65\tlist; later blocks degrade to `HEAD` scope — records still push, scoped to\n66\tthe checked-out branch. And a custom namespace's hook only fires if its\n67\t`cliName` is on PATH or `hookInvocation` was given; otherwise its owner\n68\tsyncs through the library.\n69\t\n70\t## Size policy\n71\t\n72\tRecords carry pointers, digests, and spans — never large artifacts. Git notes\n73\treplicate to every clone that fetches the ref; a checkpoint, a media file, or\n74\ta whole database belongs elsewhere, referenced by path + hash (see\n75\t`resolved`). The redaction stack walks `content` and `raw.data` only, which\n76\tis the second reason not to smuggle payloads into other fields.\n77\t","type":"edited_text_file"},"injection_type":"attachment/edited_text_file"},"context":{"branch":"annals-extraction","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"88b10fb5683696dc24ca942f505bc42d4fa3fff7","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-782115b1cc3b23539f12d21b1dd8f5ed7a75e80f44fa4d4441926ffe9ba67027","kind":"con